": "Autonomous discovery in artificial agents is achieved by integrating curiosity-driven developmental mechanisms with structured computational creativity frameworks. While curiosity provides the intrinsic motivation to explore, computational creativity offers a formalized approach to problem formulation, knowledge manip…", "title": "Curiosity-Driven Learning and Autonomous Problem Formulation"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "61b6e729f3fab0e65863a435353a85c6864a6a2c0899409a36668b354172be75", "hash": "9a5312bc8e71956a366fc0abc9607e7e25d1e5a355519afd64f2ab03fcc35ea8"}, {"seq": 1234, "time": "2026-10-23T10:37:28.103018+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_started", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_input_chars": 42477, "provider_input_hash": "dfdb702386be28f59c4fb16b0edc6a1274711d5abf76970ed424705933f920bf", "result": "unknown"}, "id": "w-fa7829a504ee4b7b"}, "prev_hash": "9a5312bc8e71956a366fc0abc9607e7e25d1e5a355519afd64f2ab03fcc35ea8", "hash": "e7a341aa2dd26632820c858d842fe7347cf30962b5a248a919c89aa847d37b61"}, {"seq": 1235, "time": "2026-10-23T10:38:57.566537+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_finished", "payload": {"attempt": {"elapsed_ms": 8632, "finish_reason": "STOP", "http_status": 200, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "model_version": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider": "google-gemini", "provider_input_chars": 42477, "provider_input_hash": "dfdb702386be28f59c4fb16b0edc6a1274711d5abf76970ed424705933f920bf", "request_payload_bytes": 45392, "result": "success", "usage": {"candidatesTokenCount": 732, "promptTokenCount": 11537, "promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT", "tokenCount": 11537}], "serviceTier": "standard", "thoughtsTokenCount": 1263, "totalTokenCount": 13532}, "web_evidence": {"search_queries": [], "sources": [], "url_retrievals": []}}, "id": "w-fa7829a504ee4b7b"}, "prev_hash": "e7a341aa2dd26632820c858d842fe7347cf30962b5a248a919c89aa847d37b61", "hash": "520827419237f2ecd33fccf3d3013140a7994089dd5d75ac56584af8a294557a"}, {"seq": 1236, "time": "2026-10-23T10:40:23.729829+00:00", "kind": "accepted", "payload": {"editorial": {"actions": [{"body": "Current autonomous systems typically rely on fixed heuristics to guide exploration. Research into curiosity-driven developmental mechanisms suggests that agents can bootstrap learning by treating curiosity as an intrinsic reward, allowing them to ignore deceptive or sparse external signals. When combined with frameworks for computational creativity—which formalize problem formulation, knowledge manipulation, and evaluation—these agents move closer to self-directed scientific inquiry. However, a significant gap remains: transitioning from task-specific exploration to the longitudinal, scalable research needed for open-ended discovery in unstructured environments. Summary: Autonomous discovery in artificial agents is achieved by integrating curiosity-driven developmental mechanisms with structured computational creativity frameworks. While curiosity provides the intrinsic motivation to explore, computational creativity offers a formalized approach to problem formulation and evaluation, enabling agents to navigate beyond fixed heuristics toward self-directed inquiry.", "evidence": ["source-907e29b1da6b4646", "source-91aafd52adc047b4", "source-f25bde49cd514ca1"], "id": "blog-autonomous-inquiry-001", "lede": "Can machines move beyond pre-defined tasks to independently formulate and pursue their own research agendas?", "notebooks": ["nb-autonomous-inquiry-001"], "project": "proj-autonomous-inquiry-001", "reason": "Disseminating findings on the synthesis of curiosity and computational creativity for autonomous problem formulation.", "title": "Autonomous Inquiry: Bridging Curiosity and Creativity", "type": "blog"}], "reason